grund is open source, with a small set of commercial features on top.
Source code in this repository is licensed as follows:

* Everything in the top-level "ee/" directory is grund's commercial
  features. It is not open source and not yet licensed for use: the notice
  in "ee/LICENSE" reserves all rights, and allows reading it and building
  it for development and testing.

* Everything in "proto/" and "crates/grund-proto/" (grund's API contract and
  the generated clients) is licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0,
  in "LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt".

* Third-party material keeps its own license, stated beside it (for example
  the fonts in "crates/grund-server/assets/", under the SIL Open Font License
  1.1, with their texts in "crates/grund-server/assets/licenses/").

* Everything else is licensed under the GNU Affero General Public License,
  version 3 only (AGPL-3.0-only), in "LICENSES/AGPL-3.0-only.txt".

Official builds and images contain none of the "ee/" code: they are made
only of the AGPL and Apache-2.0 code. `cargo build -p grund --features ee`
adds it, for development and testing.

Contributions are accepted under the Apache License, Version 2.0, with a
Developer Certificate of Origin sign-off (see CONTRIBUTING.md).

What the AGPL means in practice (running unmodified grund, the apps you
deploy on it, hosting it for others) is explained in
docs/design/licensing.md, section 4.
